{"id":"sh/0fipwzip","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":204,"width":629,"height":91},"text":"Play Barnard’s Star’s comparison. Its bright glow shifts north against surrounding stars between August 2025 and August 2026.","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/ni98rehg","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":310,"width":629,"height":37},"text":"2  Check the explanation","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/mh07y90v","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":355,"width":629,"height":118},"text":"The pair uses nearly the same wavelength. The shift agrees in direction and approximate size with the catalog prediction. The saturated core limits precise position measurements.","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/9krqtozm","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":490,"width":629,"height":37},"text":"3  Keep a reasoned conclusion","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/8jip0ji1","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":535,"width":629,"height":126},"text":"The student records what changed, what it supports and what remains uncertain. A reference helps them reflect. The saved evidence lets a teacher revisit the observations behind the answer.","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
